course: dictionary
lesson: 2469
title: Words with many meanings: dash
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the sentence tells you which one you need. «The rabbit dashes past him.» Here dashes means runs very quickly. Ask yourself: what would fit in this sentence?
explain: «Add a dash of milk to the sauce.» A dash here is a very small amount, not a run. Swap in your meaning, "a small amount of milk", and check that it still makes sense.
explain: In writing, a dash is a short line that marks a pause or an extra thought: «The answer was simple – or so she thought.» It is longer than a hyphen, which joins words, as in well-known.
fact: As a noun, a dash is a short, fast run. As a verb, to dash means to run or go very quickly.
fact: «A dash» can be a short race, like the 100-metre dash.
fact: In writing, «a dash» (–) shows a sudden break or an extra thought.
fact: «A dash of salt» means a very small amount.
fact: «To dash hopes» means to end them.
exercise: «The rabbit dashes past him.» What does dashes mean here? | Makes a short line in writing | Ends the story | Adds a little salt | *Runs very quickly
exercise: «Add a dash of milk to the sauce.» What does dash mean here? | A long race | To run away fast | A short line in writing | *A very small amount
exercise: «Rain dashed their hopes of a picnic.» What does dashed mean? | Painted | *Ended | Spelled out | Started a race
test: «The answer was simple – or so she thought.» What does the dash show? | A fast run | A small amount | *A pause or an extra thought | A minus sign in a sum
test: Which one is a 100-metre dash? | A splash of paint | A short line in writing | *A short, fast race | A long walk up a hill
exam: Sam says dash always means running. Is he right? | *No, it can also mean a small amount, a short race or a pause mark | Yes, a dash always means running fast | No, it only means a line on a map | Yes, but only in writing
